laurel 2996: LAUREL TIMER COALESCING: the kernel's timer coalescing is off from the first frame (Scion 8782070); both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/gpu.md "Timer coalescing".

[V Scion S9] CoreAnimation ran at exactly 10 frames a second from mk_timers that fired up to 100 ms late: with mach_timer_coalescing_enabled
a timer of a thread that is not real time is slid by its class (timer_coalesce_bg_ns_max 100 ms for the background tier, 75 ms and more for
the low latency tiers; arm_timer.c). The window server's frame timer and every client's display link are such timers. The switch is the one of
sysctl kern.timer_coalescing_enabled; the framebuffer turns it off as its vsync timer starts. Kill switch laureltcoal=0. One line.

